-- AI Marking Assistance v1 — question-level marking guides (additive) —
-- see docs/ai-marking-assistance-v1.md and prisma/schema.prisma's
-- Question.aiMarkingGuide comment for full field documentation.
--
-- Generated by comparing against:
--   npx prisma migrate diff --from-schema <schema at commit 2bf1284> --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script
-- (a genuine schema-to-schema diff, not --from-empty — this project has
-- no prisma/migrations history to diff from-empty against safely, and a
-- direct two-schema diff produces exactly the real delta with no
-- database connection required to generate it).
--
-- Additive only — ONE new nullable column on the existing Question
-- table. No existing table, column, constraint, row, enum value, or
-- index is changed, removed, or renamed. No new table, no new enum.
--
-- New column: Question.aiMarkingGuide (nullable TEXT). NULL means "no
-- guide configured" (the value for every existing row), in which case AI
-- marking assistance falls back to the existing auto-generated default
-- rubric. Non-null is an optional, lecturer-authored marking guide,
-- owned by the question and reused automatically for every student's
-- answer to that question, by both the single-answer (POST
-- /api/lecturer/submissions/[id]/answers/[questionId]/ai-mark) and
-- exam-wide bulk (POST /api/lecturer/exams/[examId]/ai-mark-essays)
-- AI-marking endpoints. Read/written only by LECTURER-authorized routes
-- for the owning exam — NEVER serialized to a STUDENT-facing response
-- (see the route audit in docs/ai-marking-assistance-v1.md). Editing
-- this value never mutates any existing Answer.aiReasoning snapshot
-- (historical evidence of what was actually used for a specific past AI
-- draft).
--
